## Adaptive Quality

### Network-Based Limits

| Network | Max Resolution | Max Streams | Bitrate Cap |
|---------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| 3G / slow | 480p (SD) | 1 stream | 1 Mbps |
| 4G / LTE | 720p (HD) | 2 streams | 4 Mbps |
| WiFi | 1080p (FHD) | 4 streams | 10 Mbps |
| WiFi (5GHz) | 1080p (FHD) | 6 streams | 20 Mbps |

### Implementation Strategy
```dart
// Monitor connectivity and adjust quality
final networkQualityProvider = StreamProvider<NetworkQuality>((ref) {
  return ConnectivityService.networkQualityStream;
});

// Player auto-adjusts based on network quality
class AdaptiveStreamManager {
  void onNetworkChanged(NetworkQuality quality) {
    switch (quality) {
      case NetworkQuality.poor:
        _limitResolution(480);
        _limitConcurrentStreams(1);
        break;
      case NetworkQuality.moderate:
        _limitResolution(720);
        _limitConcurrentStreams(2);
        break;
      case NetworkQuality.good:
        _limitResolution(1080);
        _limitConcurrentStreams(4);
        break;
      case NetworkQuality.excellent:
        _limitResolution(1080);
        _limitConcurrentStreams(6);
        break;
    }
  }
}
```

### Bandwidth Detection
- Measure download speed on app startup and periodically.
- Use HLS variant playlist to auto-select appropriate quality.
- Expose manual quality override in player UI.

## Player State Management

### State Model
```dart
@freezed
class PlayerState with _$PlayerState {
  const factory PlayerState.idle() = _Idle;
  const factory PlayerState.connecting({required String cameraId}) = _Connecting;
  const factory PlayerState.buffering({required String cameraId}) = _Buffering;
  const factory PlayerState.playing({
    required String cameraId,
    required StreamProtocol protocol,
    required VideoQuality quality,
  }) = _Playing;
  const factory PlayerState.paused({required String cameraId}) = _Paused;
  const factory PlayerState.error({
    required String cameraId,
    required String message,
  }) = _Error;
  const factory PlayerState.disposed() = _Disposed;
}
```

### Player Notifier
```dart
class PlayerNotifier extends Notifier<PlayerState> {
  @override
  PlayerState build() => const PlayerState.idle();

  Future<void> startStream(String cameraId, StreamProtocol protocol) async {
    state = PlayerState.connecting(cameraId: cameraId);
    try {
      // Initialize player based on protocol
      // ...
      state = PlayerState.playing(
        cameraId: cameraId,
        protocol: protocol,
        quality: _currentQuality,
      );
    } catch (e) {
      state = PlayerState.error(
        cameraId: cameraId,
        message: _mapStreamError(e),
      );
    }
  }

  void stopStream() {
    _disposeCurrentPlayer();
    state = const PlayerState.idle();
  }
}
```

